    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80-a1">

                <pb facs="0154" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1861/pg154"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baldwin to Mr. Adderley</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Richmond</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Virginia</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-07-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 30, 1861</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Adderley</hi>: The secretary of the navy of
                    the Confederate States of America has ordered from England, to be shipped to
                    Nassau, a quantity of arms and powder. I have recommended them to be consigned
                    to you, and <pb facs="0155" n="155" xml:id="pg155"/> I have to ask of you, as a
                    favor to me, to take good care of them. I will be with you soon, and will expect
                    your aid in transhipping the same.</p>
                <p>I must request you to regard this as a confidential communication, and will
                    explain the reasons when we meet. You need not write me at all on the
                    subject.</p>
                <p>Hoping soon to see you, I remain your friend,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. P. BALDWIN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Adderley</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Nassau, N. P., Bahamas</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
